Viscosity Is Not Flow​
Why coupled transport determines the manufactured package​
The title is direct and slightly provocative. It immediately introduces the misconception we want to correct.

Central thesis​
Viscosity is a material property describing resistance to deformation. Flow is the actual motion that occurs when pressure, capillary force, gravity, moving boundaries, or another mechanism acts on that material inside a particular geometry.

Temperature, shear rate, filler distribution, and cure state may change the material’s apparent viscosity. Pressure and geometry then determine whether, where, and how rapidly it flows.

The resulting flow establishes the physical structure that remains after assembly:

TIM bond-line thickness;
underfill coverage;
filler distribution;
trapped voids;
wetting and contact;
cured geometry;
residual stress.

That realized structure then determines thermal resistance, warpage, yield, and reliability.

Strong deterministic chain​
The essay should follow one clear physical sequence:

Material state → viscosity and rheology → driving mechanism → velocity field → manufactured geometry → thermal and mechanical performance → reliability

